  "details": "I’ve been dealing with a severe amount of online harassment in VRChat, and I don’t think people realize how serious it can get.  This isn’t just random trolling. I’ve been doxxed, targeted, and harassed repeatedly. It has gone far beyond the game — my real life, my family, and the people close to me have been affected by this.  Every day I log in, or even when I’m offline, I’m reminded of the things people say about me. Lies, insults, personal attacks — it builds up. It’s exhausting, and honestly, it’s reached a point where it makes me want to break down.  I joined VRChat because I wanted to create, not to deal with this. I never cared much about social attention — I just wanted to build and enjoy the platform. But now, people who think they “know” me are spreading things and causing real damage.  Despite everything, I’m trying to stay strong. But not everyone can handle this kind of pressure. Situations like this can push people toward depression or worse. This isn’t something to take lightly.  The truth is, this hurts deeply. I really love this game, and that’s what makes it even harder. But right now, I just can’t keep going like this.  So today, I’m stepping away from VRChat for a while. I need that distance.  I also want to say this clearly: harassment and doxxing are not “drama” or “part of the internet.” They are serious issues. And it shouldn’t be on players to “deal with it” alone — this is something that requires real support and accountability.  If you’re part of this community, please understand that behind every avatar is a real person. What you say and do has real consequences.  And to anyone else going through something similar: you’re not alone. I know how hard it is.  I just hope things change.",
